23
00:01:54.795 --> 00:02:01.077
Methods should be described well enough for
readers to evaluate the work.

24
00:02:01.077 --> 00:02:09.056
Consider this worked case: Students document
exact software versions, dataset sources, and

25
00:02:09.056 --> 00:02:13.045
step-by-step procedures for their thesis
experiment.

26
00:02:13.045 --> 00:02:20.655
Follow every arrow in order and name the state
before and after each transition.

27
00:02:20.655 --> 00:02:26.373
The trace converts an abstract statement into
an inspectable sequence.

28
00:02:26.373 --> 00:02:33.777
Name each dependency explicitly, and keep
labels and representations consistent

29
00:02:33.777 --> 00:02:35.998
throughout the analysis.

30
00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:42.904
Next, compare the choices involved in Ethical
Computing Standards and make the decision

31
00:02:42.904 --> 00:02:43.947
criteria explicit.

32
00:02:43.947 --> 00:02:47.009
Computing professionals should avoid harm.

33
00:02:47.009 --> 00:02:54.337
Consider this worked case: Students include a
section in their proposal detailing how they

34
00:02:54.337 --> 00:02:58.525
